From 65f688302da024cac70f2d6a91f27b8259fb0b89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:08:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] draft(A6-41 item 1): tsc pendingExpressions flow, member
 passes, outerThis placement, safe extends, named evaluation

standard_decorators.rs (transformESDecorators port):
- pendingExpressions owned by the visitor, saved/restored by the class and
  other frames; every decorated member queues its decorator array assignment
  in source order; visitReferencedPropertyName absorbs the queue into the
  member's computed name, visitComputedPropertyName absorbs it into the next
  non-inlineable computed name (decorated or not); leftovers become leading
  static-block statements after _metadata, projected through _outerThis.
- class decorators are transformed before the extends expression (both in
  the enclosing frame); class decorators keep lexical this.
- two member passes (non-constructors, then constructors), each member under
  a class-element frame with balanced enter/exit on Ok and Err paths.
- hoisted var temporaries precede let _outerThis (mergeLexicalEnvironment).
- safeExtendsExpression: (0, expr) for anonymous class/function/arrow.
- named evaluation sources (variable, parameter, binding element, property
  assignment, shorthand, assignment operators, export assignment, class
  property incl. non-literal computed names through the __propKey temp).
- decorator call binding takes the receiver's range on the assignment and
  its parentheses; the injected constructor body is a fresh multi-line block;
  updated computed names are updates of the parsed name node.

Witness group decorator-transform-order: 10/60 -> 32/60 exact twice
(target/dec-next-runs/item1-r3); residuals are nested temp numbering,
_outerThis numbering and the class-fields cache-assignment finder on
comma-list computed names, addressed by the following commits.
