+# A6-41 decorator-next: visit order, super paths, name owners (isolated draft)
+
+Purpose: implement and verify the A6-41 rows left open after the receiver-frame
+draft (`h2-8a-decorator-receiver-frames.md`): decorator/heritage/member visit
+order with tsc's `pendingExpressions`, the decorated-class `super` paths, the
+generated-name owners, and the visit-cache / receiver-identity assumptions.
+This is an isolated research candidate in the worktree
+`~/dev/tsc-rs-dec-next` (branch `draft/h2-8a-decorator-next`); root production,
+hosted acceptance and whole-H2.8 completion are out of scope.
+
+Pinned source: `vendor/typescript-6.0.3/lib/_tsc.js`, whole SHA-256
+`1c59e77a54b186ec43fa7f3e0d3c4bb15ca5eb5ba43e96b1d3a267139eddd3e3`
+(`transformESDecorators` 98946–100620, named evaluation 93715–93960,
+`isNamedEvaluation` 15917–15985).
+
+## Start point
+
+Commit `cb4e5f3e8` on the draft branch = `6e298cda8` + the attempt65 archive
+`source-and-inputs.tar.gz` (SHA-256
+`60be6b2790c600be85907ed6446168c3449a11e5d0711525cf39ae76ee005592`, the
+`prelaunch.archive` of `ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-receiver-emitter-checks.v1.json`).
+All 1014 inputs and 109 vendor inputs of that prelaunch manifest match byte for
+byte; the two archived design documents were restored to their `6e298cda8`
+versions (they are not build inputs). Production file SHA-256 at the start:
+`standard_decorators.rs` `7872d2f6…dfe0`, `class_fields.rs` `c423c244…8081`,
+`class_fields/downlevel.rs` `506ea986…0b9`. The existing 36 receiver-context
+commands reproduce 36/36 exact twice on this start point (own target dir,
+demoted; log `target/dec-next-runs/baseline-context/run.log`).
+
+## Witnesses (fresh TypeScript, twice, diagnostic-free)
+
+Three new complete-command groups, generated by
+`scripts/generate-decorator-next-witness-inputs.py` (ES2015/ES2022/ESNext ×
+set/define like the receiver-context fixture), observed by
+`scripts/observe-decorator-next-witnesses.mjs <group> --write` (two
+repetitions, zero exceptions, zero reported diagnostics) and compared as
+complete commands (JS, maps, diagnostics, emit result, write callbacks, status,
+exit, partial writes) by the contracts module
+`crates/compiler/tests/integration/h2_8a_decorator_next_witnesses.rs`
+(`TSC_RS_DECORATOR_NEXT_CASE_SET=transform-order|super-paths|name-owners|all`,
+`TSC_RS_DECORATOR_NEXT_CASE_FILTER=<substring>`).
+
+| group | commands | fixture SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| decorator-transform-order | 60 (10 sources) | `c831b004c92557b383d19e364829ae960f65361a8253a24a1f53aa4248c8a4ae` |
+| decorator-super-paths | 42 (7 sources) | `7ef1f767d49eb7f3c89008ba1120a4e93f9de2f1c063bd550c9988fdb0e998de` |
+| decorator-name-owners | 24 (4 sources) | `9cc04b4a69e083a0660f7709b5e84b12a9e3a92acb66744fe23448149905a71e` |
+
+`decorator-super-paths/*/super-undecorated-control` is an adjacent control for
+the class-fields owner (no decorators at all); `super-member-decorated-only`
+has member decorators but no class decorator (no `classThis`, so
+`transformESDecorators` leaves `super` alone). ESNext/define commands keep the
+decorators native (tsc emits `@dec` unchanged there; the standard-decorator
