+## Upstream facts used by the implementation
+
+- `transformClassLike` transforms class decorators first, visits the extends
+  expression second (both in the enclosing frame, before `enterClass`), then
+  visits non-constructor members and constructors in two passes, each member
+  under its own class-element frame.
+- `pendingExpressions` (saved/cleared by `enterClass` and depth-0
+  `enterOther`, restored on exit) receives `_x_decorators = [...]` for every
+  decorated member in source order; a decorated member with a non-literal
+  computed name absorbs the queue into `[(…, _a = __propKey(expr))]`
+  (`visitReferencedPropertyName`), and any later computed name whose visited
+  expression is not simply inlineable absorbs it too
+  (`visitComputedPropertyName`), decorated or not. Whatever is left after the
+  members becomes expression statements right after the `_metadata`
+  declaration of the leading static block; only those statements get lexical
+  `this` replaced by `_outerThis` (`let _outerThis = this` unshifted before the
+  class-definition statements, after the hoisted `var` temporaries of
+  `mergeLexicalEnvironment`).
+- Class decorators keep lexical `this` (the IIFE is an arrow); a static
+  property's decorators are visited with `classThis` (`this.dec` →
+  `_classThis.dec`).
+- `safeExtendsExpression`: an anonymous class expression, anonymous function
+  expression or arrow function in the extends position becomes
+  `(0, expression)`.
+- Hoisted temporaries restart at `_a` in every nested lexical environment
+  (nested class IIFE, static property initializer IIFE, static block) and the
+  temp sequence skips `_i` and `_n`.
+- Named evaluation of an anonymous decorated class expression: variable,
+  parameter, binding element, shorthand property, assignment (`=`, `&&=`,
+  `||=`, `??=`) and property assignment names give `__setFunctionName(_classThis,
+  "<name>")`; a class property with a non-literal computed name hoists the
+  `__propKey` cache temp and names the class by it
+  (`static [_c = __propKey(keys.a)] = (() => { … __setFunctionName(_classThis, _c) … })()`).
+  A decorated computed property whose initializer is a decorated class hoists
+  the same generated name twice (`var _b, _b`); not reproduced (open row).
+- `_outerThis` is `Optimistic` without `FileLevel`/`ReservedInNestedScopes`:
+  numbered in print order across the whole file (`_outerThis`, `_outerThis_1`,
+  … across siblings and nested classes) and against source identifiers and
+  global names. FileLevel names (`_classThis` unless a static private/accessor
+  member exists, `_metadata`, `_classSuper`, `_classDecorators`, …) collide
+  with source identifiers and with `hasGlobalName` of other files
+  (`var _classThis = 1` in a script file gives `_classThis_1` everywhere).
+- `super` in decorated static initializers/blocks (with `classThis` and
+  `classSuper`): `Reflect.get(_classSuper, key, _classThis)`, `.call(_classThis,
+  …)`, `.bind(_classThis)` for tagged templates, `Reflect.set(…)` with a
+  hoisted result temp when the value is used, compound/logical assignment
+  through a stabilized key temp, pre/postfix updates through
+  `expandPreOrPostfixIncrementOrDecrementExpression`, destructuring targets
+  through `({ set value(_a) { Reflect.set(…) } }).value`. Temporaries hoist
+  into the static block or, for a property initializer, into an IIFE
+  `(() => { var …; return …; })()`.
